' ============================================================================
'  gifdemo.cut -- animated GIFs on a layer.
'
'  An animated GIF is just art: `show <layer> "<file>.gif"` and it plays. No
'  `anim`, no frame count, no fps, no splitting the file into a PNG sequence.
'  The engine decodes every frame at load and plays each at ITS OWN delay, so
'  the GIF looks exactly as it does in any other viewer.
'
'  Why the engine carries its own decoder: _LOADIMAGE will happily open a .gif
'  and hand back only the FIRST FRAME. The handle is valid, every existence
'  check passes, the lint is clean -- and the picture never moves. That is
'  indistinguishable from a still the author meant to be still, which is why it
'  had to be fixed at the decoder rather than papered over.
' ============================================================================

scene gifdemo
dev                      ' a showcase, not a story beat: kept out of the Storybook
storybook "Animated GIFs" "Drop a .gif on a layer and it plays itself."

var body$ = "dungeon-mode.ttf"

stage 2112x1632
show bg "bg/cham-wizlab.png" fill
cam 0.5,0.5 zoom 1.5
async pan to 0.5,0.62 over 18.0 ease inout

font  body$ 20
color #e8e2d0
music "everdark" fadein 2.0

title "ANIMATED GIF" "one file, every frame" for 2.5

' -------------------------------------------------------------- ONE GIF
' A SPRITE wants `scale`. `fit`/`fill` size against the STAGE, which is right
' for a backdrop and wrong for a rune -- and they ignore `scale` when both are
' given, so the linter warns rather than letting it silently fill the screen.
show rune "rune-pulse.gif" scale 2.4 at 0.5,0.55 fade 1.0
say "That rune is a |14single .gif|07 on a layer. Eight frames, playing at the delays baked into the file."

' ------------------------------------------------------- SEVERAL AT ONCE
' Each layer runs its own animation, independently -- they are separate
' decodes, so they do not have to share a frame or a rate.
show r2 "rune-pulse.gif" scale 1.3 at 0.24,0.42 fade 0.8
show r3 "rune-pulse.gif" scale 1.3 at 0.76,0.42 fade 0.8
say "Layers animate independently. These three are the same file, decoded three times."

' ------------------------------------------------- IT IS STILL A LAYER
' A GIF layer is an ordinary layer: it moves, scales, fades and parallaxes
' like any other, and keeps animating throughout.
async move r2 to 0.24,0.70 over 4.0 ease inout
async move r3 to 0.76,0.70 over 4.0 ease inout
say "It is a |10layer|07 like any other -- it moves, scales and fades while it plays."

async grow rune to 3.4 over 3.0 ease back
say "Growing it does not stop it. The frames keep coming."

async fadelayer r2 to 0 over 2.0
async fadelayer r3 to 0 over 2.0
say "And fading one out fades the animation with it."

waitall
hide rune fade 1.2
musicstop fade 1.5
iris in at 0.5,0.55 over 1.5
